    "8. Evidence and method"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Live reads, 2026-09-25"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ", public read-only endpoints, no keys, in two passes. Pass 1: ArcGIS REST ",
      {
       "children": [
        "?f=json"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " field lists and a few value samples for NYS Tax Parcels Public, Monroe ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Parcels_Public"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", Rochester ",
      {
       "children": [
        "TaxParcel2024"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", Norfolk, Haldimand, Brant, St. Catharines, Niagara Falls, Welland, Hamilton, NES; NEI 2017/2019/2022 CSV headers via HTTP Range; EPA Envirofacts ",
      {
       "children": [
        "tri_facility"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "; Census CBP ",
      {
       "children": [
        "variables.json"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". Pass 2: Hamilton licence tables, Welland licence and heritage layers, NYS DEC registries, BOA and Brownfield CIP, Niagara heritage, Haldimand flood limit (layer 31), NPCA's ArcGIS Online services (fields, counts, item metadata), the PSEZ shapefile (DBF read), FEMA flood zones via an ArcGIS Living Atlas mirror, and NPRI via the ECCC data mart's real API (",
      {
       "children": [
        "data-donnees.az.ec.gc.ca/api"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", found in the page's JavaScript bundle; CSV headers by Range). Raw responses were kept in the session scratchpad, not in the repo."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Still not read:"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " the MPAC product itself (not held); FEMA's authoritative host (",
      {
       "children": [
        "hazards.fema.gov"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " reset the connection on three paths); the NPCA licence PDF (the item's link returns 404); Niagara County NY parcels (still ",
      {
       "children": [
        "Token Required"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " on a re-check); CBP data queries (need an API key); NYS Building Footprints layer 0 (index moved); NPCA owner values (deliberately not sampled) and the MPAC property-code table. The ledger now has no ",
      {
       "children": [
        "unverified"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " or ",
      {
       "children": [
        "catalog_only"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " rows; the remaining ",
      {
       "children": [
        "documented"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " rows are repo-doc evidence not re-read live."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
